     mmaaiill..llmmttpp reads the standard input up to an end-of-file and delivers it
     to an LMTP server for each _u_s_e_r's address.  The _u_s_e_r must be a valid user
     name or email address.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd _d_e_s_t_i_n_a_t_i_o_n
             Specify the destination LMTP address.

     --ff _f_r_o_m
             Specify the sender's name or email address.

     --ll _l_h_l_o
             Specify the LHLO argument used in the LMTP session.  By default,
             mmaaiill..llmmttpp will default to "localhost".

